	(text "Connector: J50 module cable (ULX3S side), J51 debug header, bench test points."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 38.1 12.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c4498244-57ef-4383-8317-ef9f887ea0b7")
	)
	(text "Design intent (Rev A revision 3, 2026-10-09, decisions 12 and 13; nothing here is simulated or measured)\n\n+5V_CABLE (PROPOSED, decision 13): J50 pins 1 and 2 are the system rail, renamed from +5V. It is the priority input of the Power sheet source mux U5 (TPS2121);\n  the module never sources it, and with USB-C also attached the cable powers the module and USB carries data only.\n\nULX3S target pairs (PROPOSED; ULX3S schematics v3.1.7 p.2, Lattice FPGA-TN-02032 v1.4 p.14, p.26):\n  First choice gp/gn[8..13] (bank 7, left), second choice gp/gn[14..21] (banks 2/3, right).\n  Do not use gp/gn[0..7] or [22..27]: banks 0/1 have no differential input and no on-die termination.\n  Constrain the true pad (gp) only; gn is the complement. Do not guess polarity: swap in gateware if reversed.\nLVDS termination rule (PROPOSED; docs/research/ulx3s-lvds-input.md s.3): terminate at the FPGA with DIFFRESISTOR=\"100\".\n  R180 (100R) is DNP and bench-only (scope or test load with no FPGA attached).\n  NEVER fit R180 with DIFFRESISTOR on: two 100R loads make ~50R and cut VOD by about half (arithmetic, not measured).\n  No series capacitors and no pull-ups on the pair (TLV3605 output is DC-coupled at ~1.2 V common mode, TLV3605 DS p.7).\n  ECP5 LVDS input common-mode range: UNRESOLVED (FPGA-DS-02012 not obtained).\nCAN rule (PROPOSED; docs/research/module-controller.md s.3, SLLA270 p.4, p.8): NO termination on the module.\n  One split termination (2 x 60R 1% + 4.7 nF to ground) sits at the FPGA-end junction only; modules are plug-in, so a\n  module-end resistor would leave with the module and load the star (120/N ohm). R182/R183/C180 here are DNP\n  and for a single-module bench setup only; never fit them on a module that joins a star.\n  Bit rate 125 kbit/s (8 us bit), PROPOSED; verify on the bench at G1/G2.\nAUX / AUX2 (PROPOSED): J50.12 -> R186 1k -> AUX and J50.11 -> R187 1k -> AUX2, both bidirectional to the Controller\n  (reserved ESP32 GPIOs, undefined function). The old HOLD_N buffer (U50, R184, R185, C181) is removed in revision 2.\n  SHDN_N and LE_HYS are driven from the Controller sheet; no pull-ups here.\nHV rule (PROPOSED): no bare APD_BIAS pad on this sheet. HV_MON (~Vout/101, unbuffered 10 M / 100 k divider with 10 nF,\n  source impedance ~100 k) is the ONLY HV observation point."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 150 205 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "856fa4b4-3be0-4443-854d-a18bb442857d")
	)
	(text "J50 MODULE CABLE pinout (Wuerth 61201221621, 2x06 shrouded, 2.54 mm; PROPOSED,\ndocs/research/module-controller.md s.6; pins 2n-1/2n share a row)\nRow 1:  1 +5V_CABLE  2 +5V_CABLE  system supply rail (mux priority input on Power, never sourced by the module)\nRow 2:  3 GND      4 GND      power return\nRow 3:  5 LVDS_P   6 LVDS_N   50 Mbps pair on adjacent pins (twisted pair)\nRow 4:  7 GND      8 GND      ground row between LVDS and CAN\nRow 5:  9 CAN_H    10 CAN_L   CAN pair\nRow 6:  11 AUX2    12 AUX     reserved control lines, each 1k to the Controller (ESP32 GPIOs)\nPin 12: research doc proposes SPARE (wire to GND at both ends if unused); the spec makes it AUX."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 200 20 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "784c7bea-3a7f-4c5c-a92d-35cd52d675a8")
	)
	(text "J51 DEBUG pinout (2.54 mm, 1x6)\n1  GND\n2  RSSI     received-signal strength (Monitor sheet)\n3  AUX2     after R187 1k\n4  AUX      after R186 1k\n5  HV_MON   ~Vout/101, only HV observation point\n6  3V3_D    digital rail"
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 240 120 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4c72375a-ef7d-413e-ab2a-71a6df94b709")
	)
